# 12. ADAPTIVE AI PRACTICE ENGINE

This is one of the core differentiators.

Build an intelligent question-selection system that prioritizes students' weak topics.

## How It Works

Analyze:

- Previous scores.
- Mistake frequency.
- Topic accuracy.
- Recent performance.
- Revision history.
- Question difficulty.

## Example

A student repeatedly performs poorly in Newton's Laws.

Instead of generating completely random physics questions, ExamDNA should recommend additional verified questions from that concept.

## Question Selection

For a 10-question adaptive quiz:

- Approximately 60% weak-topic questions.
- Approximately 25% developing-topic questions.
- Approximately 15% strong or unassessed-topic questions.

Adjust these percentages when enough eligible questions are unavailable.

Avoid repeating identical questions unnecessarily.

Allow students to compare improvement across attempts.

